# NOTICE — Provenance and third-party credits

## Origin

Catfish-Pi is derived from **GooeyPi** — https://github.com/am-will/gooey-pi
(MIT License, © GooeyPi contributors). The initial codebase was taken from the
GooeyPi v1.1.15 snapshot (2026-09-02) and renamed. The upstream copyright
notice is preserved in `LICENSE` alongside the Catfish-Pi copyright.

The vendored Prime Agent artifacts under `vendor/` keep their upstream
`0.7.0-gooeypi.1` version strings: those patch releases were produced and are
documented by the GooeyPi project (see `vendor/prime-agent-0.7.0-gooeypi.1.md`
and `vendor/prime-agent-ai-0.7.0-gooeypi.1.md`).

## Design borrowing from the OMP/Pi desktop ecosystem

Catfish-Pi's initial code absorbs advantages identified in a source-level
survey of sibling community projects (research dated 2026-10-11). Credits:

| Project | What Catfish-Pi takes | Status |
|---|---|---|
| [apoc/omp-desktop](https://github.com/apoc/omp-desktop) (MIT) | Minimum harness version floor that refuses outdated agents with an explicit update command, instead of failing as silent protocol drift | **Implemented** (`electron/main/harness-version.ts`, `docs/harness-discovery.md`) |
| [GooeyPi](https://github.com/am-will/gooey-pi) (MIT) | Entire base: four-layer multi-harness abstraction, OMP `negotiate_protocol` v2 handshake with `rpc_chunk` reassembly, omp/pi event normalization, 256-byte title-slot session readers, MCP settings-lock writer, capability extension injection | Base code |
| [oh-my-pi-gui](https://github.com/nornzach/oh-my-pi-gui) (MIT) | Bundled agent sidecar packaging (`bun --compile` + `extraResources` + runtime resolution) as the distribution reference | Reference |
| [ompweb](https://github.com/nguyencanhtrung/ompweb) | RPC v2 frame/chunk bounds (1 MiB frames, 64 MiB reassembly) and session-JSONL race-avoidance patterns; equivalent defenses already exist in the GooeyPi base | Cross-checked |
| [Pi Desktop](https://github.com/FaqFirebase/pi-desktop) (Apache-2.0) | omp/pi protocol difference checklist (event spellings, `get_fork_messages` absence, `models.yml`) used as adapter assertions | Reference |
| [jeffscottward/omp-web](https://github.com/jeffscottward/omp-web) | `omp acp` / ACP v1 integration quality reference | Reference |
| [oh-my-pi-desktop](https://github.com/dylansantwani/oh-my-pi-desktop) (MIT) | Crash-recovery pattern (backoff + generation guard + two-phase kill) | Reference |

"Reference" means the idea informed Catfish-Pi's design without copying code;
the named projects' licenses govern their own code.

